{
  "summary": "The RNA-only, single-profile PCA baseline achieved a validation accuracy of 0.4849 and F1 of 0.4639, indicating that RNA features alone provide a usable but modest predictive signal. This result establishes an initial reference point for future RNA encoder, profile, or multimodal comparisons. It remains uncertain whether this accuracy reflects the inherent predictive power of RNA, the PCA representation, or the single-profile setting, because no comparative experiments have been completed."
}

